Source: @DISTRO_ID@-hybrid-backlight
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: @DISTRO_HOME_URL@
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: @DISTRO_ID@-hybrid-backlight
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, udev, systemd
Description: hide the phantom NVIDIA backlight device on hybrid laptops
 On laptops whose internal panel is driven by the integrated GPU, the NVIDIA
 driver still registers a backlight device (nvidia_0) with its own scale.
 Brightness tools that pick the first device or rescale between devices then
 set the wrong brightness, and the driver re-registers the device after every
 resume from suspend. This package shadows the phantom device's sysfs directory
 with an empty tmpfs whenever a backlight device appears, and leaves it alone
 when the NVIDIA GPU drives the panel itself.
